So `ValueEncoder.encodeBits` casts to `(Float)` for F32 properties. If a reactive property yields an Integer where F32 is expected, it'd ClassCastException. So my `ReactiveValues.from` must coerce to the property's value type.

Note `ReactiveValues.from` already maps Boolean→Integer (1/0) which is used for U8/U32 properties (VISIBLE, ENABLED, UNDERLINE, etc.). But if a Boolean is used for a F32 property, it'd be Integer → wrong. Boolean props are all U8 currently. Good.

But e.g. `ALIGNMENT` is F32; config stores `Signal<HorizontalAlignment>` → WireValue → returns `(float)` ✓. Good.

`GRID_COLUMNS`/`GRID_ROWS` — not in the switch → default F32. Config stores `Signal<Integer>` → ReactiveValues returns Integer → encodeBits casts (Float) → CCE! So I need columns/rows to yield Float. 

Simplest: make `ReactiveValues.from` coerce numeric based on property type:
```java
int type = ValueTypes.forProperty(property);
if (type == F32) {
    if (value instanceof Float f) return f;
    if (value instanceof Integer i) return (float) i;
    if (value instanceof WireValue w) return (float) w.wire();
    ...
}
```
Let me rewrite ReactiveValues.from to coerce by declared type:
- F32: Float stays; Integer→(float); WireValue→(float)wire; Boolean→(float)(1/0)? unlikely.
- U8/U32/I32/ENUM: Integer stays; Float→? (SELEcted is set from Boolean→int). Boolean→1/0; WireValue→wire.
- COLOR: Color; String token? Color has token.
- STRING: String.

Let me implement a robust `from`:
```java
public static Object from(int property, Signal<?> signal) {
    Object value = signal.get();
    if (value instanceof Boolean b) value = b ? 1 : 0;
    else if (value instanceof WireValue w) value = w.wire();
    return coerce(property, value);
}
private static Object coerce(int property, Object value) {
    int type = ValueTypes.forProperty(property);
    switch (type) {
        case ValueTypes.F32: return toFloat(value);
        case ValueTypes.U8, ValueTypes.U32, ValueTypes.I32, ValueTypes.ENUM: return toInt(value);
        case ValueTypes.COLOR: case ValueTypes.STRING: case ValueTypes.DESIGN_TOKEN: return value;
        default: return value; // LIST etc. — not reactive property values
    }
}
```
`toFloat`: Float→f; Integer→(float); WireValue→(float)wire; Boolean→1/0f; else throw.
`toInt`: Integer→i; Float→? (e.g., ACTION_ID expects U32; config stores Signal<Integer> → ok); Boolean→1/0; WireValue→wire; else throw.

But wait: `CONTENT_MODE` is F32 and config stores `Signal<ContentMode>` → WireValue → int, then toFloat → float. Good.
`SHAPE_KIND` F32; WireValue → float. Good.
`ALIGNMENT` F32; WireValue. Good.
`GRID_COLUMNS` F32; Integer → toFloat. Good.
`LINE_LIMIT` U32; config Signal<Integer> → toInt. Good.
`ACTION_ID`/`BINDING_ID` U32; Integer. Good.
`SELECTION` U32; Picker uses `node.property(SELECTION, WritableSignal<Integer>)`? Actually Picker sets `node.properties.put(SELECTION, selection.get())` + propertyBindings. Let me unify picks later.
`VALUE`/`MIN_VALUE`/`MAX_VALUE`/`PROGRESS`/`GAUGE` F32; config Signal<Float> → Float. Good.
`OPACITY` F32; Float. Good.
`WIDTH`/`HEIGHT` F32; Float. Good.
`FIXED_SIZE_*` U8; config Signal<Boolean> → Boolean→1/0 → toInt. Good.
`IS_INDETERMINATE` U8; set via int.
`TEXT_STYLE` F32; Font uses Modified.prop with float (static). If reactive, wire.
`ROLE`/`STATE` F32 (default) — config Signal<Integer> → toFloat. Good (ROLE/STATE ride as F32? ValueTypes default F32). Actually ROLE/STATE aren't in the switch → default F32. And previously AccessibilityRole put `(float) value`. Good, so toFloat(Integer). ✓.
`PICKER_STYLE`/`TOGGLE_STYLE`/`DATE_PICKER_MODE` F32; WireValue → float. Good.
`FONT_WEIGHT`/`FONT_SIZE`/`FONT_WIDTH`/etc F32; config Signal<Float>. Good.

Great, so coercing by declared type fixes the GRID_COLUMNS issue and is generally robust.

But note: existing static puts (e.g., Grid previously `(float) columns`) are Float — still fine.

Also `Modified.Prop` static path: `ReactiveValues.from` is only used for reactive props. Static props use the raw value directly. So static Integer for GRID_COLUMNS would still be wrong, but we keep static as Float. Fine.

